# Architecture

- Preserve the established separation: data access in `src/sanity/lib`, presentational components in `src/components`, page shells in `src/app`.
- Presentational components must not fetch content.
- Page components must not contain long inline GROQ queries; use `src/sanity/queries`.
- Provider/data normalization stays separate from UI rendering.
- Do not bypass TypeScript with `any`.
- Secrets and server-only credentials never belong in client components or `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variables.
- Cloudinary CDN URLs in `MediaRenderer` use plain `img` tags, not the Next.js image optimizer.
- Do not hard-code fake portfolio projects as production content.
- Preserve this architecture unless there is a clear, documented reason to change it.
